# W44-156 distance-aware variant Z A/B (2026-05-21)

## Status

[SHIPPED] — production default `W44_156_VARIANT_Z_D_HIGH_THRESHOLD = 5.5`

## Setup

- Host: lilith (AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB)
- Date: 2026-05-21
- Parent commit: `6739107c` (W44-155 spot-check + diagnosis)
- Build: `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --features '__expert butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel' --example w44_156_distance_aware_variant_z_ab`
- cjxl reference: `/home/lilith/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl` (v0.12.0)
- Decode: jxl-oxide (linear request)
- Metrics: butteraugli (Rust crate, linear input), fast_ssim2 (sRGB u8 input)

## Source

Follow-on to W44-155 (`6739107c`, measurement-only) which diagnosed the
1420710 e5 d=6 OPEN cell: our model over-consolidates into DCT32X32
(78.6% of first-blocks at d=5 vs cjxl 51.8%) and doesn't shed small
blocks at the d=5→d=6 transition (DCT8: cjxl 39→16, ours 10→2).
Per-region qac is AT PARITY — pure strategy selection issue.

W44-155 recommended distance-aware variant Z: weaker dct32x32 lift
(~1.18-1.20) above d~5.5, keep W44-154's 1.22 below.

## Mechanism (SHIPPED)

3 new `EntropyMulTable` constructors in `src/effort.rs`:
- `high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_d_high`        (plain Z d-high, dct32x32=1.20)
- `high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_high_colour_d_high` (Z' d-high, dct32x32=1.20, dct16x32=1.30)
- `high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_low_colour_d_high`  (Z'' d-high, dct32x32=1.20, dct16x32=1.23)

New constant in `src/vardct/encoder.rs:286`:
- `W44_156_VARIANT_Z_D_HIGH_THRESHOLD: f32 = 5.5`

Env hook in `src/vardct/encoder.rs:498`:
- `__JXL_W44_156_THRESHOLD` — runtime override (0.0 = disable, any
  positive value = use as threshold). Production default 5.5.

Dispatch at BOTH variant Z dispatch sites (`compute_ac_strategy` and
the inner `profile_for_search` site):
```rust
let w44_156_d_high = w44_96_variant_z && self.distance > w44_156_effective_threshold();

p.entropy_mul_table = if w44_98_variant_z_high_colour {
    if w44_156_d_high {
        EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_high_colour_d_high()
    } else {
        EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_high_colour()
    }
} else if w44_99_variant_z_low_colour {
    if w44_156_d_high {
        EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_low_colour_d_high()
    } else {
        EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_low_colour()
    }
} else if w44_96_variant_z {
    if w44_156_d_high {
        EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z_d_high()
    } else {
        EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z()
    }
} else { /* default W44-29 suppressed */ };
```

Mirrors the W44-98/99 sub-discriminator pattern (HC / LC split inside
variant Z, gated on `m3_colourfulness`) but adds a distance-axis split
that's orthogonal to the colour-axis split.

## Bisect design

20 cells × 3 variants paired interleaved (60 encodes total):

| Class                   | n | Cells                                       |
|---                      |---|---                                          |
| TARGET                  | 1 | 1420710 e5 d=6                              |
| PROTECT_1531677_d6      | 3 | 1531677 d=6 × e7/e8/e9                      |
| PROTECT_1420710_d45     | 6 | 1420710 d=4/5 × e7/e8/e9                    |
| PROTECT_1531677_d5      | 3 | 1531677 d=5 × e7/e8/e9                      |
| PROTECT_1418519         | 4 | 1418519 d=5/6 × e8/e9 (variant Z doesn't fire) |
| PROTECT_codec_wiki_d3   | 1 | codec_wiki e8 d=3 (variant Z doesn't fire)  |
| CONTROL_NOGATE          | 2 | 1189261/1044329 photos off variant Z gates  |

Variants:
- **A = baseline** (no d-high split; equivalent to W44-154 ship)
- **B = threshold 5.5** (d > 5.5 → d-high; SHIPPED)
- **C = threshold 5.0** (d > 5.0 → d-high)

## Headline results

### Aggregate (vs A baseline)

| Variant            | Δvs_cjxl (B) | n   | FIXED→OPEN | OPEN→FIXED | Δssim2_avg | ssim2_min/max |
|---                 |---           |---  |---         |---         |---         |---            |
| A_baseline_no_split| -20680B      | 20  | 0          | 0          | +0.0000    | [+0.00, +0.00]|
| **B_threshold_5p5**| **-21089B**  | 20  | 0          | 0          | -0.0286    | [-0.19, +0.00]|
| C_threshold_5p0    | -21089B      | 20  | 0          | 0          | -0.0286    | [-0.19, +0.00]|

**B == C empirically** on this cell coverage (no cells fall in the
(5.0, 5.5] range where they would differ). The 5.5 threshold is the
safer ship (narrower d-high band).

### TARGET closure

| Variant | bytes_pct | bfly_pct | closed? |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | +4.115% | -0.743% | true (bfly axis) |
| **B** | **+2.739%** | **-0.743%** | **true (BOTH axes — bytes now also < 3%)** |
| C | +2.739% | -0.743% | true (BOTH axes) |

W44-156 closes the TARGET cell on bytes axis (was at +4.115% under
W44-154 baseline; now at +2.739% under B/C). The cell was already
technically "closed" on bfly axis at the baseline (bfly_pct -0.743%
< 3.0%) but W44-153 ledger criterion requires BOTH bytes_pct AND
bfly_pct > 3.0% to mark OPEN; with bytes at +4.115% the cell sat at
the edge of the FIXED/OPEN boundary depending on how the ledger
applies the OR vs AND rule. W44-156 moves it firmly into FIXED on
both axes, eliminating ambiguity. The W44-155 diagnosis predicted
this — the W44-154 1.22 lift over-fires DCT32X32 at d=6 (relative
to cjxl's d=6 strategy distribution); the W44-156 1.20 d-high lift
matches cjxl's distribution better.

### Per-class deltas (B vs A)

| Class                   | n | Δssim2_avg | Δbytes_avg | verdict |
|---                      |---|---         |---         |---|
| TARGET                  | 1 | -0.0337    | -278.0B    | bytes improved, SSIM2 within budget |
| PROTECT_1531677_d6      | 3 | -0.1797    | -43.7B     | bytes improved, SSIM2 -0.18 (within 0.30 budget) |
| PROTECT_1420710_d45     | 6 | +0.0000    | +0.0B      | **byte-identical** (d=4/5 ≤ 5.5, gate off) |
| PROTECT_1531677_d5      | 3 | +0.0000    | +0.0B      | **byte-identical** (d=5 ≤ 5.5, gate off) |
| PROTECT_1418519         | 4 | +0.0000    | +0.0B      | **byte-identical** (mask=76 fails W44-29 mask<50) |
| PROTECT_codec_wiki_d3   | 1 | +0.0000    | +0.0B      | **byte-identical** (screenshot path, not Z) |
| CONTROL_NOGATE          | 2 | +0.0000    | +0.0B      | **byte-identical** (off W44-96 gate) |

### Worst-case SSIM2 deltas

Worst SSIM2 drop is -0.192 on 1531677 e8/e9 d=6 — within the 0.30
budget. These are also the cells where bytes IMPROVE (-46 to -49B
each). Pareto-positive trade.

